{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "miradore",
  "description": "One page from the site-path endpoint. Proves the wrapped list containers (<Tags>/<Tag>, <InvApplications>/<InvApplication>, <InvStorages>/<InvStorage>) are read -- reading the singular name as a direct child of <Device> finds nothing and silently drops software, tags and storage. Also proves the dd.MM.yyyy parse, the LocalIPAddress spelling, an application with no Identifier still building (Software requires an id), a Deleted device and an ID-less device being skipped, 127.0.0.1 never reaching an interface, and a future LastReported being clamped instead of failing the record. Request 1 is the path probe. The configured page size of 500 must be clamped to 10 because application inventory is on: a page of devices with their applications is ~34x larger, and one page holding a whole estate exceeded the Explorer's memory limit and reported nothing.",
